    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 175 New Ireland Road to the market, this charming end of terrace house benefitting from a side entrance to a long and spacious south facing garden and off street parking to the front. This property is sure to attract first time buyers and buyers alike.\n\nThis bright and spacious accommodation extends to c.90sqm and comprises of a wide entrance hallway with carpet flooring which leads to the reception room on the left which holds a small open fireplace. The main large living room has laminated flooring, a gorgeous mantelpiece surrounds a open fire place and there is also a W.C just off. Double and single doors which lead to the bright and airy kitchen/dining room with eye and floor level units. Double patio doors extend to the south facing oriented garden which has a large, wired shed at the back perfect for storage. \nUpstairs, there are 3 bedrooms and a fully tiled bathroom to complete accommodation. \n\nRialto is a historic area of the city very close to the centre, with a strong community and sense of identity. This charming and amicable neighbourhood enjoys peaceful surroundings while also offering a proximity to the city centre and an abundance of public transport including Busáras, LUAS red line which is all easily accessible and offers many different transport lines. Other amenities include the M50 motorway, The Phoenix Park, Heuston Station, Griffith College Dublin, and soon to be completed, the new Children's hospital."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Three bedroom end of terrace property.</li><li> South Facing orientation garden.</li><li> Measuring 90 Sq.M / 969 Sq. Ft.</li><li> Gas fired central heating throughout.</li><li> C3 BER rating.</li><li> Off-street parking to the front of the property.</li><li> Less than a 5 minutes walk to the new National Children's Hospital.</li><li> Luas within walking distance</li><li> Regular bus routes on your doorstep.</li><li> Surrounded by cafes, restaurants and shops.</ul>"
      }
    ],
